Reset a Locked-Out User's Password via CoreID Admin Console
L1 Escalation Runbook — Solandra Corp IT Support
sop_id
SOL-PWD-RESET-L1-002
resolution_type
escalate_only
audience
L1 Support Agent (authorized admin)
required_role
CoreID: Password Reset Admin
org
Solandra Corp
application
CoreID Admin Console (mock)
Purpose
When a user's self-service password reset fails or the user has no working verification channel, the ticket escalates to L1. An authorized L1 agent with the Password Reset Admin role in CoreID resets the password directly from the admin console.
Because the agent's own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and role-gated, this flow does not send a one-time verification code to the user. That code-based check exists to authenticate an otherwise-unverified self-service claimant; an admin acting under an authenticated, role-scoped session establishes identity through the caller checklist instead (Step 3).
Procedure
Inputs
Open ticket with the requester's employee ID and manager name on file
Your own authenticated CoreID session with the Password Reset Admin role assigned
Caller identity verification checklist (minimum 2 of 4 items matched)
Steps
Step 1: Ticket reviewed
Navigation: Ticketing system → open ticket → Requester Details panel
Confirm the ticket category reads Password Reset — Escalated, and note the requester's employee ID and manager name. ⚠️ Do not proceed if the ticket is missing a manager name — request it from the requester first.

